"Paul Scarr","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10949","person_slug":"paul-scarr","vote":"no"},{"name":"Penny Allman-Payne","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11002","person_slug":"penny-allman-payne","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ralph Babet","party":"United Australia Party","person_id":"tvfy_11003","person_slug":"ralph-babet","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"no"}],"name":"Criminal Code Amendment (Hate Crimes) Bill 2024 - in Committee - Minimum age of offenders","noes":28,"question":"The majority voted against [amendments](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2025-02-06.89.1) (2) and (4) to (9) on sheet 3259, which were introduced by Victorian Senator [Lidia Thorpe](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/victoria/lidia_thorpe) (Independent). This means they were not successful. The amendments would have added minimum age requirements so that these offences do not apply to to people under 14 years old. ### Amendment text > *(2) Schedule 1, at the end of item 10A, at the end of section 80.2A of the Criminal Code, add:* > >> *Offences do not apply to persons under 14* >> >>> *(7) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if the first person is under the age of 14.* > > *(4) Schedule 1, at the end of item 18A, at the end of section 80.2B of the Criminal Code, add:* > >> *Offences do not apply to persons under 14* >> >>> *(8) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if the first person is under the age of 14.* > > *(5) Schedule 1, item 19, after subsection 80.2BA(7), insert:* > >> *Offences do not apply to persons under 14* >> >>> *(7A) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person if person is under the age of 14.* > > *(6) Schedule 1, item 19, after subsection 80.2BB(8), insert:* > >> *Offences do not apply to persons under 14* >> >>> *(8A) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if the first person is under the age of 14.* > > *(7) Schedule 1, item 19, at the end of section 80.2BC of the Criminal Code, add:* > >> *Offences do not apply to persons under 14* >> >>> *(9) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if the first person is under the age of 14.* > > *(8) Schedule 1, item 19, at the end of section 80.2BD of the Criminal Code, add:* > >> *Offences do not apply to persons under 14* >> >>> *(10) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if the first person is under the age of 14.* > > *(9) Schedule 1, item 19, at the end of section 80.2BE of the Criminal Code, add:* > >> *Offences do not apply to persons under 14* >> >>> *(8) Subsections (1) and (2)","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9534","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2025-02-06/16"}
